.TH OPENVPN3-GUI 1 "October 2026" "OpenVPN 3 GUI 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openvpn3-gui \- desktop interface for OpenVPN 3 Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openvpn3-gui
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-\-tui ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OpenVPN 3 GUI provides native GTK screens for profiles and sessions,
forms for all commands and options exposed by the installed openvpn3
CLI, and an interactive terminal for credentials and live logs.
Run it as the normal desktop user, without sudo.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Display sample profiles and simulate commands without touching real VPN
profiles, sessions, or network connections. CLI help is still read locally.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Launch the terminal interface without loading graphical libraries.
.SH NOTES
Closing the application does not disconnect established VPN sessions.
Use My VPNs to disconnect. Configuration exports may contain private
keys and are saved with owner-only permissions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openvpn3 (1),
.BR openvpn3-config-import (1),
.BR openvpn3-session-start (1)

.SH APPEARANCE AND TRAFFIC
Use the header menu button to hide or show navigation. Appearance defaults to
System, following the desktop preference. Light and Dark overrides are saved in
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/openvpn3-gui/preferences.json (normally ~/.config).
Demo mode does not persist appearance settings.
.PP
The connection card samples transport bytes for the selected connected session
approximately every two seconds and plots the last 60 seconds. Counters include
VPN overhead. Traffic history stays in memory. After disconnect, the card shows
the last recorded snapshot; final CLI statistics are in Last action details.

.SH SYSTEM TRAY
The status icon provides per-session status, quick connect, disconnect,
pause/resume, refresh, open-window and quit actions. Closing the window keeps
the app in the tray only when a StatusNotifier host is available.
Disable this behavior under About & help, System tray. Ctrl+Q requests a full
exit. Quitting does not disconnect established VPN sessions.
.PP
If the tray host disappears while the window is hidden, the window reopens.
GNOME may need an AppIndicator extension; no extension or login autostart is
configured automatically. Connecting and resuming show authentication prompts
in the main app. Demo mode does not persist the close-to-tray preference.
